Marvel Ultimate Alliance 2's shadow pass at 1x with DLSS and FSR 3.1. Before its scene, MUA2 draws two shadow maps
into pitch 1040 1x surfaces (D24S8 depth bases 1216 and 1632, 512x512 viewports with the lights' projections, no pixel
shader except for casters that also write color at base 0), resolves them to 1024x1024 and 1024x512 textures, and
filters each into a k_16_16 copy at color base 0 that the scene's draws sample; after the scene, the same pitch and
sample count holds a 1024x32 texture its composite reads. The mua2 profile names that surface
(native_pre_scene_key): its draws before the scene are one PreSceneTargets surface and its draws after it another
(kAfterScene), so the 1024x32 texture no longer keeps the shadow pass at the full scale. Once 0162 and 0164's checks
prove it only an input of the scene, its draws before the scene go to 1x in every mode, with the game's own depth
bias, and its resolves are stretched to the textures' full size; only after a frame that drew the scene, and back to
the full scale for the session if a draw after the scene samples one of its textures. Every other surface keeps the
full scale for mua2, among them the 4x quads that clear the shadow maps (covering the 1x ones) and the scene's memory,
the bloom chain, the composite, HUD and menus. mua1 and mua1-gold leave native_pre_scene_key unset, so their surfaces,
scales and logs are 0162 and 0164's. The GPU targets line lists a surface once per scale and adds each one's share of
host pixels.

